<title>POLAND: Polish MPs ask to end duty-free grain imports.</title>
<headline>Polish MPs ask to end duty-free grain imports.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish parliament's Agriculture Committee asked the government to immediately reinstall duties on grain imports, due to remain duty-free until mid-1997, the Rzeczpospolita daily said on Saturday.</p>
<p>It also said that over the last three months the Agriculture ministry several times unsuccessfully appealed to the government to limit the scope of the duty-free grain imports to aid domestic farmers.</p>
<p>The government lifted duties on grains and rapeseed to June 1997 last November to help keep food prices down.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
